-- title:
--   Label units: uᵃ ∈ Jⁿ with exact exceptional order
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime and $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. The field $L$ has characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and `hι` requires that there be a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((T))$ is, by `hK`, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the level group [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133).
--
--   The ring $A$ is a discrete valuation domain, Henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field; `hAq` puts $q$ into $\mathfrak m_A$ and `hζA` requires $\zeta$ to lie in the image of $A$. The field $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and, by `hj`, has Laurent expansion the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function. The element $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and `hϖt` requires $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\cdot(\text{unit})$ in $A$. Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec} C \leftarrow \operatorname{Spec}(\cdot) \rightarrow \operatorname{Spec}(\text{chartAlgInf})$. The ideal $y$ of $C$ is maximal (`hy`) and contains $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and `hss` is a supersingularity condition at $y$: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Say that $\tau \in \operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ is a *level automorphism attached to* $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ when [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) holds; unfolded, this requires that for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) having integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ with $p_g$ giving a non-zero Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$ under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i /q}$, the product of the coefficientwise $\iota$-image of the expansion of $\tau x$ with the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, where [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.conjElemN q δ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L13) is the matrix with rows $(\delta_{00}, \delta_{01}/q)$ and $(q\,\delta_{10}, \delta_{11})$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is a rigidified local-chart assumption at all supersingular points of $X$ above the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$: for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ and satisfying the same supersingularity condition `hss'` as `hss` but for $y'.asIdeal$, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u\big)$, satisfying seven clauses, summarised here: $e$ carries the image of $a \in A$ to the class of the constant $\sigma a$; every level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; if in addition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then the induced endomorphism of $C$ is the identity modulo $y'.asIdeal$; for every such $\gamma$ and $\tau$ whose induced endomorphism of $C$ is the identity modulo $y'.asIdeal$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ transporting the action of $\tau$ on $C$ through $e$ and the germ map at $y'$, fixing the constants, acting on the classes of $X_0, X_1$ by $M$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by their classes, with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, with $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak m_W}$ whenever $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak m_W}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ avoiding the classes of $X_0, X_1$, containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$ and having linear parts $(a_1,b_1)$, $(a_2,b_2)$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ contract to distinct ideals of the stalk; for a prime with linear part $(1,0)$, an element $a \in C$ lies in the contracted ideal exactly when all Laurent coefficients of $a$ lie in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; and finally [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-expansion with parameter replaced by its $q$-th power) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and after subtracting a suitable $a_0 \in A$ its image in $S$ equals the class of a power series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0 \ge 1$, whose degree-$e_0$ form takes unit values at every pair $(a,b)$ from $W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   Next a single such point is fixed: $z$, the germ $\varpi_z$ with `hϖz` and `hz` as above, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `hy'` and the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y` identifying $y'.asIdeal$ with $y$; together with data $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ of exactly the shape produced by `hArig`, and the hypothesis `hW₁`, which asserts for these data the same list of clauses (with $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$) as in `hArig`.
--
--   The ideal $J$ of $C$ is, by `hJ`, the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $(\tau|_C)^{-1}$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ (\text{completion}) \circ (\text{germ at } y')$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, as $\gamma$ ranges over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma$ that preserve $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is, by `hB`, the $C$-subalgebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$, that is $C[J/\varpi_t]$. The valuation subring $W$ of $K$ contains $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` states that $C \subseteq B$ and that every element of $K$ is a ratio of elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator; `hR2` states that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` has five clauses: an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$; and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ outside $\mathfrak m_W$, in the sense that $f \in W$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak m_W$. The hypothesis `hEQ` has five clauses, summarised here: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k_A`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k_A[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q _ - 1`) whose kernel is the set of elements of $B$ in $\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with $A \to k_A$, and which is equivariant for every level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, via an element $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) — the kernel of $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$ — acting through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives the elements of $B \cap \mathfrak m_W$ under some level automorphism attached to some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such automorphisms lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and a level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally a subring $O$ of $K$ is given, with `hO` requiring a non-zero $a \in J$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a := C[J/a]$ (formed as for $B$, with $a$ in place of $\varpi_t$) such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, every element of $y$ that lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B \not\subseteq O$; further `hOW` gives $O \subseteq W$, `hOloc` that $O$ is local, `hOnoe` that $O$ is Noetherian, and `hCO` that $C \subseteq O$. The hypothesis `hIgStab` states that every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is $A$, which contains $\varpi$ in its maximal ideal, which contains $C$, and for which some $c \in C$ has the property that $p(c)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic $p \in A[T]$, is preserved by every level automorphism attached to any $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that $f \in V \iff \tau f \in V$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts: for every $u \in C$ with $u \ne 0$ in $K$ such that
--   (i) $u$ divides a power of $\varpi$ in $C$, i.e. $u\,z_0 = \varpi^k$ for some $k \in \mathbb{N}$ and $z_0 \in C$;
--   (ii) $\tau u = u$ for every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$;
--   (iii) for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is $A$ and in which $\varpi$, if it lies in $V$, lies in $\mathfrak m_V$, such that $j \in V$, every monic polynomial over $A$ evaluated at $j$ is a unit of $V$, and $O \subseteq V$, the element $u$ is a unit of $V$ (it does not lie in $\mathfrak m_V$); and
--   (iv) for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ satisfying the same first conditions on $L$, $\varpi$ and $j$ but with some element of $O$ lying outside $V$, the element $u$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$ whenever it lies in $V$;
--   there exist natural numbers $a, n$ with $a \ge 1$ and $n \ge 1$ such that $u^a \in J^n$ and $\varpi_t^{\,n} \cdot (u^a)^{-1} \in W$, the inverse being taken in $K$.
--
--   This is the Rees-placement step for the auxiliary level-one frame with guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$: a unit of the Igusa-type valuation rings dominating the end $O$, vanishing on those that do not, is placed exactly in the filtration by powers of the weighted centre $J$ of the supersingular blow-up, with matching order in $\varpi_t$. It is proved from [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_igusaType_valuationSubring_not_le_end_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_igusaType_valuationSubring_not_le_end_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd), and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_verticalUnit_chartAlgFin_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_verticalUnit_chartAlgFin_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd) in the analysis of the vertical components of the integral model at a supersingular point.
